{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792481634,"nonce":"YgbORNuBYxkQpDaUWmBf99/sZS8=","title":"GpuPaintContext applies layer opacity to children before compositing it again","message":"Source-confirmed while testing 5c9ff267e5f19ea41e0d9e28404a954b7bf2fa092cbdc6abef731a98001321d4. GpuPaintContext::push_layer pushes config.opacity onto opacity_stack and records the same config in LayerCommand::Push. combined_opacity multiplies that stack; brush_to_colors and apply_opacity_to_brush bake it into child alpha. Layer-aware renderers subsequently multiply by config.opacity at composition.\n\nReproduction to add as a producer regression: create GpuPaintContext, push LayerConfig::new().opacity(0.5), fill an opaque red rectangle, pop, take_batch. The primitive alpha is 0.5 and the recorded group opacity is 0.5. A layer-aware renderer therefore produces 0.25 contribution instead of the intended 0.5. Overlapping children also receive the group factor individually before the group composite. This inference is from source and emitted-data logic; producer pixels were not reproduced in the overlay-entry-point slice.\n\nThe pre-existing render_with_layer_effects and render_overlay_with_layer_effects already composite config.opacity. Fixing render_overlay_msaa's missing layer walk makes this producer mismatch relevant there too. Raw PrimitiveBatch layer tests with opaque child colours correctly get group opacity exactly once; the producer must emit the matching contract.\n\nInvestigate push_layer/pop_layer opacity ownership alongside explicit push_opacity and nested layers, and verify static, dynamic and composite routing. Do not simply disable GPU group opacity, which would break overlapping children and raw batch callers. Keep any broader layer-command routing changes separate from the already-closed auxiliary payload routing issue 5571d817c0d8c5003fc2f0c6f4b1928596a2ace51d4f247469e234f20741ed16. This is a producer follow-up, not a widget/state architecture migration.","files":null}]}